## Changes

Issue 137: history preparation projected every action before approved-actions
could omit actions without cards. A NULL ID became zero in previous-value
lookup and raised an unrelated history error. Projections now skip NULL IDs
and IDs absent from the prepared card-info map. Raw actions and changes remain
retained; existing readable action cards still use the original projection
and missing-create diagnostics. The reader's permission filter is unchanged.

Issue 138: the discarded page preparation rendered action summaries against
the same mutable diff objects as the served page. Preparing a page view now
uses a separate disposable diff memo, restored in `finally`. Served and bare
renders retain their existing shared action memo. Whole-engine cache reset
now clears that retained memo as its documented lifetime requires. The three
discarded page/modal preparations use this boundary. Partial test engines
continue to use their render stub. No changes to the diff algorithm, toggle
ordering, fixtures, expected bytes or issue 110's rename logic.

